{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And to You</b> — Afterward he praises HaShem that He shows kindness to the children of man, and He warns them and makes known to them that He repays a man according to his deed. And some say: \"For You,\" even though [it lacks the kaf of comparison], in the manner of: \"For it is a stiff-necked people\" (Exodus 34:9). In the end, \"to You is kindness.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:33.456023121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}